# Line endings are LF everywhere, including on Windows checkouts.
#
# Not a style preference. The files under `crates/node/src/ui/` are embedded
# with `include_str!` and served to browsers byte for byte, so a CRLF checkout
# would make a Windows-built binary serve different bytes than a Linux-built
# one. For a project handing out unsigned binaries with a provenance
# attestation, "the same source produces the same output" is worth more than
# matching the platform's convention.
#
# It also stops a test that matches across a newline from passing on two
# platforms and failing on the third.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything that is not text, so git never touches the bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
